Getting Started with the LetBuyy API | LetBuyy Resources Why LetBuyy Products Themes Apps Developers Pricing Log in Start for free Start for free Resources All Ecommerce Growth Payments Operations AI Commerce Developers Changelog Commerce updates Contents 01 Authentication 02 Core Endpoints 03 Rate Limits 04 Pagination 05 Errors 10 min read Updated Jun 2026 Share Print Back to Resources Resources › Developers Featured Getting Started with the LetBuyy API Everything you need to make your first authenticated API call. A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations 18 May 2026 10 min read Updated 16 Jun 2026 Copy link Save # api # developers # integration # authentication The guide, illustrated An authenticated request connects your application to structured store data. Concept illustration Explore an idea, then read the detail. 01 Authenticate 02 Endpoints 03 Pagination Authentication The API uses Bearer token authentication. Generate an API key from Settings → Developer → API Keys in your Merchant Control Plane. Keys are scoped: read-only, read-write, or admin. Read this section Core Endpoints Explore the examples and explanation in this section. Read this section Pagination For POST requests that create resources (orders, products), send an Idempotency-Key header. If the same key is used within 24 hours, the API returns the original response instead of creating a duplicate. Read this section The LetBuyy API is a REST API with JSON responses. Every LetBuyy store has a unique site_id and can be accessed programmatically via API keys scoped to specific capabilities. Authentication Authenticate An authenticated request connects your application to structured store data. Concept illustration The API uses Bearer token authentication. Generate an API key from Settings → Developer → API Keys in your Merchant Control Plane. Keys are scoped: read-only, read-write, or admin. curl -X GET \
  https://api.letbuyy.com/v1/products \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "X-Site-ID: your_site_id" Core Endpoints Resource Endpoint Methods Products /v1/products GET, POST, PUT, DELETE Orders /v1/orders GET, PUT Customers /v1/customers GET, POST, PUT Inventory /v1/inventory GET, PUT Collections /v1/collections GET, POST, PUT, DELETE Rate Limits Standard: 100 requests per second per site Burst: 250 requests in any 5-second window Rate limit headers: X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining, X-RateLimit-Reset 429 response when exceeded — implement exponential backoff Pagination Pagination Show the product clearly, then help the buyer decide. Concept illustration GET /v1/products?limit=50&cursor=eyJpZCI6MTIzfQ

// Response
{
  "data": [...],
  "pagination": {
    "next_cursor": "eyJpZCI6MTczfQ",
    "has_more": true
  }
} Idempotency Keys For POST requests that create resources (orders, products), send an Idempotency-Key header. If the same key is used within 24 hours, the API returns the original response instead of creating a duplicate. Errors 400 Bad Request: Invalid parameters — check the error.field in the response 401 Unauthorized: Invalid or expired API key 403 Forbidden: Correct key but insufficient scope 404 Not Found: Resource doesn't exist for this site_id 429 Too Many Requests: Rate limit exceeded 500 Internal Server Error: LetBuyy error — retry with backoff Article complete Up next: Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming 11 min read Continue learning A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations Builds developer tools and writes about APIs, webhooks, and extending the LetBuyy platform. 5 articles 1 topics Developers LinkedIn All articles by Arjun Weekly Newsletter Commerce guides and platform updates Commerce Insights Weekly AI Commerce insights India growth playbooks Platform feature updates Conversion rate tactics Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS Related guides Developers Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming 11 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App 13 min read Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy 10 min read Next Developers Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming 11 min read Keep reading Recommended for you Developers Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming React to order events, payment confirmations, and inventory changes in real time. 11 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App From OAuth to your first embedded app in the Merchant Control Plane. 13 min read Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy Connect your ERP, CRM, accounting software, or custom tools to your LetBuyy store. 10 min read Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS 0 Contents Next Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event