How Liquid Themes Work on LetBuyy | LetBuyy Resources Why LetBuyy Products Themes Apps Developers Pricing Log in Start for free Start for free Resources All Ecommerce Growth Payments Operations AI Commerce Developers Changelog Commerce updates Contents 01 Liquid Syntax Basics 02 Core Liquid Objects 03 Useful Filters 04 Theme Architecture 05 Sections: The Merchant Customization Layer 12 min read Updated Jun 2026 Share Print Back to Resources Resources › Developers How Liquid Themes Work on LetBuyy Build powerful, merchant-customizable storefronts with the Liquid template engine. A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations 8 Apr 2026 12 min read Updated 9 Jun 2026 Copy link Save # themes # liquid # developers # storefront From Liquid templates to a merchant-customizable storefront. Concept illustration. The developer’s field guide Liquid is LetBuyy's template language for storefronts. It's a Ruby-inspired syntax that lets you render dynamic store data in HTML templates. Every LetBuyy theme is a Liquid theme — or a React theme with Liquid fallback. 01 Write the template Liquid Syntax Basics Read store data {{ product.title }} Illustrative storefront output Ceramic Vase A template expression becomes storefront content. Example data. {# Output — double curly braces #}
{{ product.title }}
{{ product.price | money }}

{# Tags — logic and flow control #}
{% if product.available %}
  <button>Add to Cart</button>
{% else %}
  <p>Out of Stock</p>
{% endif %}

{# Loops #}
{% for variant in product.variants %}
  <option value="{{ variant.id }}">{{ variant.title }}</option>
{% endfor %} 02 Work with store data Core Liquid Objects product — current product with title, handle, price, variants, images, metafields collection — current collection with products and metadata cart — current cart state with items, total, item count customer — authenticated customer with order history shop — store settings, currency, timezone request — URL, path, host information 03 Shape the output Useful Filters Apply a filter {{ product.title | upcase }} Illustrative storefront output CERAMIC VASE The filter transforms the display value. Example data. {{ product.price | money }}              {# ₹1,499 #}
{{ product.description | truncate: 150 }}
{{ product.title | upcase }}
{{ image | image_url: width: 800 }}
{{ product.created_at | date: "%d %B %Y" }} 04 Organise the theme Theme Architecture One theme. Reusable layers. 01 layout / The page shell 02 templates / The page type 03 sections / The configurable blocks 04 snippets / The reusable details An illustrated map of the theme files described below. layout/theme.liquid: Root HTML wrapper, includes <head> and <body> templates/*.liquid: Page-specific templates (product, collection, index, cart) sections/*.liquid: Reusable, merchant-configurable page sections snippets/*.liquid: Small reusable partials (product card, price display) assets/: CSS, JS, and image files config/settings_schema.json: Defines merchant-editable theme settings 05 Hand control to the merchant Sections: The Merchant Customization Layer Hero image Configurable section illustration Image with text Configurable section illustration Sections make themes merchant-customizable without code. Define settings in the section's schema — text, colors, images, booleans — and merchants can edit them in the visual theme editor without touching Liquid. React Hybrid Themes LetBuyy supports hybrid themes where product listing and checkout use React for interactive performance, while editorial pages (homepage, about, blog) use Liquid for fast static rendering. Article complete Up next: Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy 10 min read Continue learning A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations Builds developer tools and writes about APIs, webhooks, and extending the LetBuyy platform. 5 articles 1 topics Developers LinkedIn All articles by Arjun Weekly Newsletter Commerce guides and platform updates Commerce Insights Weekly AI Commerce insights India growth playbooks Platform feature updates Conversion rate tactics Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS Related guides Developers Getting Started with the LetBuyy API 10 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App 13 min read Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy 10 min read Previous Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App 13 min read Next Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy 10 min read Keep reading Recommended for you Developers Getting Started with the LetBuyy API Everything you need to make your first authenticated API call. 10 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App From OAuth to your first embedded app in the Merchant Control Plane. 13 min read Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy Connect your ERP, CRM, accounting software, or custom tools to your LetBuyy store. 10 min read Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS 0 Contents Next Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy LetBuyy footer LetBuyy What is LetBuyy? Pricing Start your store Ecosystem Theme guide App integrations guide Developer Docs Merchant login Resources All resources Ecommerce guides Developer Docs Changelog Support Support centre Contact us Grievance redressal Security Account access India English Legal Terms Privacy Refunds Sitemap Your Privacy Choices © 2026 LetBuyy. All rights reserved.

