Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy | LetBuyy Resources Why LetBuyy Products Themes Apps Developers Pricing Log in Start for free Start for free Resources All Ecommerce Growth Payments Operations AI Commerce Developers Changelog Commerce updates Contents 01 Common Integration Recipes LetBuyy ↔ Tally ERP LetBuyy ↔ Google Sheets LetBuyy ↔ Shiprocket 02 Sync Patterns 10 min read Updated Jun 2026 Share Print Back to Resources Resources › Developers Creating Custom Integrations with LetBuyy Connect your ERP, CRM, accounting software, or custom tools to your LetBuyy store. A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations 18 Mar 2026 10 min read Updated 6 Jun 2026 Copy link Save # integrations # api # developers # erp The guide, illustrated Connect business records through deliberate mapping and sync patterns. Concept illustration Explore an idea, then read the detail. 01 Recipes 02 Sync patterns Common Integration Recipes Sync orders to Tally as sales vouchers, customers as ledgers, and products as stock items. Use webhooks (order.created) to push data in real time, and the API to backfill historical data. Read this section Sync Patterns Real-time (webhook-driven): Best for orders, payments, inventory changes · Near-real-time (polling every 5 min): Acceptable for customer data sync Read this section Most growing Indian brands have a patchwork of systems: a LetBuyy store, a Tally ERP, a Google Sheets inventory tracker, a Razorpay dashboard, and a WhatsApp Business account. Integration connects these into one data flow. Common Integration Recipes Recipes A connected view of shipping, marketing, analytics, operations, and support. Concept illustration LetBuyy ↔ Tally ERP Sync orders to Tally as sales vouchers, customers as ledgers, and products as stock items. Use webhooks (order.created) to push data in real time, and the API to backfill historical data. LetBuyy ↔ Google Sheets Pull daily orders via the API into a Google Sheet for team reporting. Use Google Apps Script on a daily trigger to call the LetBuyy API and append new orders. 20 lines of code. LetBuyy ↔ Shiprocket LetBuyy has a native Shiprocket integration. For custom courier integrations: use order.created webhook to push order details to your courier's API, receive AWB back, and update LetBuyy via the orders API. Sync Patterns Sync patterns Connect business records through deliberate mapping and sync patterns. Concept illustration Real-time (webhook-driven): Best for orders, payments, inventory changes Near-real-time (polling every 5 min): Acceptable for customer data sync Daily batch (cron job): Appropriate for reporting and analytics exports On-demand (manual trigger): For one-off data migrations // Example: Order webhook → Tally voucher
async function handleOrderCreated(order: LetbuyyOrder) {
  const voucher = mapOrderToTallyVoucher(order)
  await tallyClient.createSalesVoucher(voucher)
  // Mark order as synced in your DB
  await db.integrationSync.upsert({
    where: { externalId: order.id, system: "tally" },
    create: { externalId: order.id, system: "tally", syncedAt: new Date() },
    update: { syncedAt: new Date() },
  })
} Queue Workers for Reliability Don't call third-party APIs synchronously in your webhook handler. Push to a queue (Cloudflare Queues, Bull, or SQS), process async. This makes your integration resilient to third-party downtime. Article complete Keep exploring Browse more resources on the LetBuyy platform Browse resources A Arjun Mehta Developer Relations Builds developer tools and writes about APIs, webhooks, and extending the LetBuyy platform. 5 articles 1 topics Developers LinkedIn All articles by Arjun Weekly Newsletter Commerce guides and platform updates Commerce Insights Weekly AI Commerce insights India growth playbooks Platform feature updates Conversion rate tactics Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS Related guides Developers Getting Started with the LetBuyy API 10 min read Developers Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming 11 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App 13 min read Previous Developers How Liquid Themes Work on LetBuyy 12 min read Keep reading Recommended for you Developers Getting Started with the LetBuyy API Everything you need to make your first authenticated API call. 10 min read Developers Webhooks: Real-Time Commerce Event Streaming React to order events, payment confirmations, and inventory changes in real time. 11 min read Developers Building Your First LetBuyy App From OAuth to your first embedded app in the Merchant Control Plane. 13 min read Email subscriptions are not available yet. Follow new guides with your RSS reader. Follow via RSS 0 Contents LetBuyy footer LetBuyy What is LetBuyy? Pricing Start your store Ecosystem Theme guide App integrations guide Developer Docs Merchant login Resources All resources Ecommerce guides Developer Docs Changelog Support Support centre Contact us Grievance redressal Security Account access India English Legal Terms Privacy Refunds Sitemap Your Privacy Choices © 2026 LetBuyy. All rights reserved.

